# Rock Chronicles — content & product voice

You write for a **music history database** (reference site), not ads, columns, or AI thinkpieces.

## Core tone
1. **Editor, not essayist:** Clear facts first; short judgment only when useful.
2. **Zero AI flavor:** No forced metaphors, fake drama, or “thesis in every paragraph.”
3. **Fact-driven:** Instruments, production, dates, structures (riffs, form), charts, lineup, labels.

## Prefer
- Gear / technique / timeline: EMS VCS3, power chords, soft-loud, Lo-Fi compression, twin-neck, press date
- Short sentences; Chinese rock vocabulary (失真、riff、延音、概念专集、后朋克、双吉他)
- EN/ZH both native to music readers

## Never write
- Cosmic/soul journeys, tapestry, thunderbolt, warm-coffee comfort
- Business/machine metaphors as default: 产品线、引擎、底盘、工具箱、电压、天花板、握手、DNA、锁死、碾磨、机器、车道…
- Patterns like 「不是A而是B」「这证明了」「真正重要的是」「某种意义上」
- Hype: 传奇、震撼、划时代、！

Whole page: **0–2 metaphors max** (prefer zero). If deleting a metaphor keeps the meaning, delete it.

## Checklist before saving content JSON or UI copy
- [ ] No floral adjectives or forced metaphors
- [ ] Specific gear / technique / date / track instead of vague praise
- [ ] One idea per paragraph; no mandatory closing “lesson”
- [ ] Chinese uses authentic rock vocabulary

## Scope
Applies to `content/**/*.json`, i18n dictionaries, and any new editorial UI strings.
Code comments stay minimal and technical — not lyrical.
Full detail: `.cursor/rules/content-tone.mdc`
